                  <handDesc>
                  <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                  <seg type="rubrication">
                    <ref target="#ms_i1.4 #ms_i1.5"/>
                  <foreign xml:lang="gez">ማርያም፡</foreign>
                  </seg>
                  <desc>Unusually the word God is not rubricated in the first three works.
                    Columetric layout of text: <locus target="#103v #104r" facs="104"/> <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur#Ps150">Mazmura Dāwit: Psalmus 150</ref>;
                    <locus target="#111v #112r #112v" facs="112 113"/> <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1566hababa#ThreeYouths3">Third Song of the Three Youths in the Furnace:  ThreeYouths3</ref></desc>
                  </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <decoDesc>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d1"><locus target="#29r" facs="029"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1012Equestrian">Equestrian Saint</ref></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d2"><locus target="#91r" facs="091"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1035HolyMan">Holy Man Portrait</ref>, a prostrate saint</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d3"><locus target="#99r" facs="099"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1012Equestrian">Equestrian Saint</ref></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d4"><locus target="#133r" facs="133"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1041HolyMen">Holy Men Potrait</ref> Three figures: Two are seated. One is <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9162TaklaHa">Takla Hāymānot</persName>, but it is not clear whether he is the one on the left or the one in the center. A third person stands to the right and holds an umbrella over the center figure. Captions (r to l): <q>“Abunä Täklä Haymanot.” “Thomas.”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="frame" xml:id="d5">
                      Decorative designs: <locus target="#1r #6v #13r #19v #28v #35v #40v #94r #115r #121r" facs="001 007 013 020 029 036 041 094 115 121"/> (haräg);
                      <locus target="#99r" facs="099"/> (lines of alternating red and black dots)
                    </decoNote>
                  </decoDesc>
                  <additions>
                    <list>
                      <item xml:id="a1">
                      <desc type="GuestText">
                      <locus target="#133v" facs="134"/> Crude attempt to copy an excerpt <title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1113Anqasa">ʾAnqaṣa bǝrhān</title>
                      </desc>
                      </item>
                      <item xml:id="a2">
                      <desc type="OwnershipNote">
                      <locus target="#60v" facs="061"/> note of ownership in a different hand, Qäñazmač Mogäs of Gojjam,
                      <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዝዳዊት፡ ዘክቡር፡ ወልዑል፡ መፍቀሬ፡ እግዚአብር፡ ርእሰ፡ መኳንንት፡ ቀኛዝማች፡ ሞገስ፡ ዘምድረ፡ ሙላዱ፡ ጐዣም፡ ዘአጥረዮ፡ በንዋዩ፡ ዘሠረቆ፡ ወዘፈሐቆ፡ ርጉም፡ ከመ፡ ዲያብሎስ፡ ያድርገው፡ አሜን፡</foreign>,
                      “This Dawit belongs to his Excellency, his highness, lover of God, head of princes, Qäazma  Mogäs. His ancestry is from Gojjam. It is purchased with his money. Anyone who steals or erases it, may he be cursed like the devil. Amen.”
                      </desc>
                      </item>
                      <item xml:id="e1">
                      <desc>
                      words of text are written interlinearly (<locus target="#19v #22v #35r #37r" facs="020 023 035 037"/>, etc.);
                      and lines of text are written interlinearly (<locus target="#38r" facs="038"/>);
                      and in the bottom margin with a symbol (┴) marking the location where the text is to be inserted (<locus target="#131r" facs="131"> f. 131r, line 7</locus>);
                      erasure markings are visible (<locus target="#2r #5v #24r #46r" facs="002 006 024 046"/>, etc.);
                      text has been removed (e.g., <locus target="#107v #124v" facs="108 125"/>)
                      </desc>
                      </item>
                      <item xml:id="e2">
                      <desc>
                      <locus target="#33v" facs="034"> f. 33v, line 12</locus>; <locus target="#60r" facs="060"> f. 60r, line 8</locus>: text is circled to signal its erasure to correct homoeoteleuton
                      </desc>
                      </item>
                      <item xml:id="e3">
                      <desc>
                      The scribe regularly has to complete a line of text on another line. Much of the problem is addressed through the selection of an
                      appropriate aspect ratio for the codex combined with an appropriate script size. But, where the line of text is still too long, the
                      scribe completes the line of text above or below the end of the line (throughout).
                      </desc>
                      </item>
                    </list>
                  </additions>
